{"game": "warframe", "language": "english", "appid": 230410, "month": "2013-12", "window": 2, "start_date": 1386460800, "end_date": 1387151999, "month_true_total": 2210, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-14 18:50:50 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "8061297", "author": {"steamid": "76561198081675887", "personaname": "Castawaye", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198081675887/", "num_games_owned": 261, "num_reviews": 11, "playtime_forever": 45182, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 6629, "last_played": 1507569311, "avatar": "7e5eb334b1040b8340f97aae7375037a82b755bc"}, "language": "english", "review": "Warframe is an interesting take on the run and gun style of third person shooters. Set somewhere in the future where technology is quite advanced and the known universe is governed by three different factions. The grinneer, corpus and the infected. You play exploring the different planets goverened by these factions in a \"Warframe\" Warframe does an excellent job blending in RPG elements with fast paced gameplay. Each Warframe has distinct abilities and purposes for different situations, I would even go as far as being to categorize them in different \"Classes\". The weapons system is also quite beautiful. Consisting of being able to upgrade and customize your weapons in any way you want. Warframe does have quite a grind which is evident later on, but if you just  want a way to waste time with three other friends, then look no further than Warframe.", "timestamp_created": 1387151077, "timestamp_updated": 1387151077, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1364234640", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "8061271", "author": {"steamid": "7656119